{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
A calque of {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|advocatus diaboli|advocātus diabolī|the devil’s advocate|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[devil]]’s [[advocate]]|pl=[[devil's advocates|devil’s advocates]]}}

# {{idiomatic}} One who [[debate]]s from a view which they may not actually hold, usually to determine its [[validity]], or simply for the sake of [[argument]].
# {{ib|Roman Catholic Church}} A [[canon]] lawyer appointed by the [[church|Church]] to argue against the canonization of the proposed [[candidate]].

